    {"object_id":"OBJ-ID-GUIDED","object_class":"GUIDED_PRACTICE","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-TRACK-001","learner_payload":"From Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu, complete: Zn maps to ______ and Cu²⁺ maps to ______ before you assign any Redox labels.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"Q-REDOX-ID-GUIDED","practice_level":"GUIDED"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-ID-GUIDED-ANS","object_class":"ANSWER","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-TRACK-001","learner_payload":"Zn maps to Zn²⁺; Cu²⁺ maps to Cu.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"ANS-REDOX-ID-GUIDED"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-MEAN","object_class":"MEANING","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":"Oxidation is an increase in oxidation state; reduction is a decrease. Compare the same element before and after the reaction.","source_ref":"CHEM-NCERT-REDOX-PRODUCTION-v1","ccbom_asset_id":"CON-REDOX-STATE-DIRECTION"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-RULE","object_class":"RULE","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":"For the governed Zn/Cu²⁺ reaction, Zn changes 0 → +2 and Cu changes +2 → 0. Increase means oxidation; decrease means reduction.","source_ref":"CHEM-NCERT-REDOX-PRODUCTION-v1","ccbom_asset_id":"CON-REDOX-STATE-DIRECTION"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-LANE","object_class":"REPRESENTATION","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":{"Zn":"0 → +2 : increase : oxidation","Cu":"+2 → 0 : decrease : reduction"},"source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"REP-REDOX-STATE-LANE","representation_type":"OXIDATION_STATE_LANE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-CHAIN","object_class":"REASONING_CHAIN","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":["Write the before oxidation state.","Write the after oxidation state for the same element.","Compare the two values.","Name oxidation only for an increase and reduction only for a decrease."],"source_ref":"CHEM-NCERT-REDOX-PRODUCTION-v1","ccbom_asset_id":"REP-REDOX-STATE-LANE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-MIS","object_class":"MISCONCEPTION_REPAIR","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":{"wrong_model":"Oxidation state is always the literal charge carried by an isolated particle.","repair":"Use oxidation state here as the governed bookkeeping value for the same element; do not confuse it with a claim about isolated particles in every compound."},"source_ref":"CHEM-NCERT-REDOX-PRODUCTION-v1","ccbom_asset_id":"MIS-OXSTATE-VS-CHARGE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-WORKED","object_class":"WORKED_EXAMPLE","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":{"Zn":"0 → +2, so Zn is oxidised.","Cu":"+2 → 0, so Cu²⁺ is reduced."},"source_ref":"CHEM-NCERT-REDOX-PRODUCTION-v1","ccbom_asset_id":"EX-REDOX-ZN-CU-STATE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-INDEP","object_class":"INDEPENDENT_PRACTICE","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":"Without looking at the completed lane, reconstruct both oxidation-state lanes for Zn + Cu²⁺ → Zn²⁺ + Cu and label each change as oxidation or reduction.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"Q-REDOX-STATE-INDEP","practice_level":"INDEPENDENT"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-STATE-INDEP-ANS","object_class":"ANSWER","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-STATE-CHANGE-002","learner_payload":"Zn: 0 → +2, oxidation. Cu: +2 → 0, reduction.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"ANS-REDOX-STATE-INDEP"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-E-MEAN","object_class":"MEANING","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":"Electron loss corresponds to oxidation; electron gain corresponds to reduction.","source_ref":"GRADE9-REDOX-SUBTOPIC-BOOK-BUILDER","ccbom_asset_id":"CON-REDOX-ELECTRON-CONSEQUENCE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-E-RULE","object_class":"RULE","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":"After proving the oxidation-state direction, write the matching electron consequence and check that electrons lost equal electrons gained.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"CON-REDOX-ELECTRON-CONSEQUENCE"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-ZN-HALF","object_class":"EQUATION","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":"Zn → Zn²⁺ + 2e⁻","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"EQ-ZN-OX-HALF"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-CU-HALF","object_class":"EQUATION","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":"Cu²⁺ + 2e⁻ → Cu","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"EQ-CU-RED-HALF"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-E-CHAIN","object_class":"REASONING_CHAIN","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":["Zn oxidation state rises 0 → +2.","That change corresponds to loss of 2e⁻.","Cu oxidation state falls +2 → 0.","That change corresponds to gain of 2e⁻."],"source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"REP-REDOX-ELECTRON-LEDGER","representation_type":"ELECTRON_LEDGER"},
    {"object_id":"OBJ-E-VERIFY","object_class":"VERIFICATION","learning_atom_id":"LA-REDOX-ELECTRON-002","learner_payload":"Electron check: 2e⁻ lost by Zn = 2e⁻ gained by Cu²⁺.","source_ref":"CT-C1A-REDOX-001","ccbom_asset_id":"VER-REDOX-ELECTRON-BALANCE"},
